FloorReplay database migrations

This directory contains the Alembic environment and revision scripts for the
FloorReplay PostgreSQL schema. backend/alembic.ini points to this directory;
env.py reads the database URL from the application settings and uses
flooreplay.models.Base.metadata, including the registered account, workspace,
review, operational receipt and paid-model tables.

Configure FLOORREPLAY_DATABASE_URL for the target database. The local default
is postgresql+psycopg://localhost:5433/flooreplay. From the repository root, run:

    make migrate

The equivalent command from backend is:

    uv run alembic upgrade head

Migrations update the schema. Load application fixtures separately with
make seed from the repository root. See ../../README.md for local setup and
../../DEVELOPMENT.md for the original coverage engine's development history.
